  "theme": "uber",
  "culturalNote": "Kamau again! This time you left your laptop bag in his car. Nairobi's Uber drivers often keep regular passengers' numbers and do favours — returning lost items, waiting, running small errands. The prepositional extension (-ia/-ea) is how you talk about favours: \"nimekuletea\" (I've brought it to you), \"nikuwekee\" (shall I keep it for you), \"ulinisubiria\" (you waited for me).",
  "startingPoint": "Evening. You realise your laptop bag is missing — you must have left it in Kamau's car this morning. You call him.",
